{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L548","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:548"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options controlling whether "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset(values)"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces the default-value\nbaseline."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"formApi.reset(savedValues, { updateDefaultValues: false })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"updatedefaultvalues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"updateDefaultValues?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional updateDefaultValues?: boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L578","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:578"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset(values)"},{"type":"text","value":" should also update the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":"\nbaseline."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, passing values to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"},{"type":"text","value":" treats those values as the new reset\nbaseline. Future "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset()"},{"type":"text","value":" calls will return to those values, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.isDefaultValue"},{"type":"text","value":" will compare against them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set this to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" when you want reset semantics for form state\n(clearing touched, dirty, validation, submission state, and mounted fields)\nbut want to keep comparing against the previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateDefaultValues: false"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.isDirty"},{"type":"text","value":" is reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":",\nbut "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.isDefaultValue"},{"type":"text","value":" may be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" if the provided reset values do\nnot deeply equal the preserved defaults."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This option is ignored when no reset values are provided."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const originalDefaults = formApi.defaultValues\n\nformApi.reset(savedDraft, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n// `savedDraft` is current, but `originalDefaults` remains the baseline.\n\nformApi.reset()\n// Restores `originalDefaults`, not `savedDraft`.","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"updatedefaultvalues","text":"updateDefaultValues?","level":3},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:548](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L548)\n\nOptions controlling whether `reset(values)` replaces the default-value\nbaseline.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nformApi.reset(savedValues, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### updateDefaultValues?\n\n```ts\noptional updateDefaultValues?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:578](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L578)\n\nWhether `reset(values)` should also update the form's `defaultValues`\nbaseline.\n\nBy default, passing values to `reset` treats those values as the new reset\nbaseline. Future `reset()` calls will return to those values, and\n`state.isDefaultValue` will compare against them.\n\nSet this to `false` when you want reset semantics for form state\n(clearing touched, dirty, validation, submission state, and mounted fields)\nbut want to keep comparing against the previous `defaultValues`.\n\nWith `updateDefaultValues: false`, `state.isDirty` is reset to `false`,\nbut `state.isDefaultValue` may be `false` if the provided reset values do\nnot deeply equal the preserved defaults.\n\nThis option is ignored when no reset values are provided.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst originalDefaults = formApi.defaultValues\n\nformApi.reset(savedDraft, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n// `savedDraft` is current, but `originalDefaults` remains the baseline.\n\nformApi.reset()\n// Restores `originalDefaults`, not `savedDraft`.\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: FormResetOptions\ntitle: FormResetOptions\n---\n\nDefined in: [FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:548](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L548)\n\nOptions controlling whether `reset(values)` replaces the default-value\nbaseline.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nformApi.reset(savedValues, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### updateDefaultValues?\n\n```ts\noptional updateDefaultValues?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [FormApi/FormApi.public.ts:578](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/FormApi/FormApi.public.ts#L578)\n\nWhether `reset(values)` should also update the form's `defaultValues`\nbaseline.\n\nBy default, passing values to `reset` treats those values as the new reset\nbaseline. Future `reset()` calls will return to those values, and\n`state.isDefaultValue` will compare against them.\n\nSet this to `false` when you want reset semantics for form state\n(clearing touched, dirty, validation, submission state, and mounted fields)\nbut want to keep comparing against the previous `defaultValues`.\n\nWith `updateDefaultValues: false`, `state.isDirty` is reset to `false`,\nbut `state.isDefaultValue` may be `false` if the provided reset values do\nnot deeply equal the preserved defaults.\n\nThis option is ignored when no reset values are provided.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst originalDefaults = formApi.defaultValues\n\nformApi.reset(savedDraft, { updateDefaultValues: false })\n// `savedDraft` is current, but `originalDefaults` remains the baseline.\n\nformApi.reset()\n// Restores `originalDefaults`, not `savedDraft`.\n```\n"}
